IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `iana-types`
IMPORT `iana-employment`
IMPORT `iana-penalty`
IMPORT `iana-offence`

-- Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "Was this employment contrary to s 15; what penalty must the employer
--    pay, and the dates on the notice and for an appeal; and is an offence
--    committed, with what maximum sentence?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Illegal working case` HAS
    `the employment`                                    IS AN `Employment facts`
    `the penalty`                                       IS A MAYBE `Penalty facts`
    `the offence facts`                                 IS A MAYBE `Offence facts`

DECLARE `Illegal working position` HAS
    `contrary to s 15`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `penalty payable`                                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `earliest pay-by date`                              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `last day to appeal`                                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `offence committed`                                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `maximum imprisonment on indictment, in months`     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `maximum imprisonment on summary conviction, in months` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 15-17, 21, 22, 24, 25
@export default The position under ss 15-25 of the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK) for an employer who employed a person: whether the employment was contrary to s 15; if a penalty notice was given, the penalty payable (s 15), the earliest pay-by date the notice may specify (s 15(6)(c)) and the last day to appeal (s 17); if the offence is in question, whether it is committed (s 21) and the maximum imprisonment on indictment and summary conviction (NOTHING where no offence). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS AN `Illegal working case`  @desc The employment and immigration position, any penalty notice and objection, and the facts for the offence
GIVETH AN `Illegal working position`
`the illegal working position for` c MEANS
    `Illegal working position` WITH
        `contrary to s 15`                              IS `the employment is contrary to s 15 in` e
        `penalty payable`                               IS
            CONSIDER c's `the penalty`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST p  THEN JUST (`the penalty payable for` e `with` p)
        `earliest pay-by date`                          IS
            CONSIDER c's `the penalty`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST p  THEN JUST (`the earliest pay-by date for` p)
        `last day to appeal`                            IS
            CONSIDER c's `the penalty`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST p  THEN `the last day to appeal for` p
        `offence committed`                             IS
            CONSIDER c's `the offence facts`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN JUST (`an offence under s 21 is committed in` e `with` o)
        `maximum imprisonment on indictment, in months` IS
            CONSIDER c's `the offence facts`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN IF `an offence under s 21 is committed in` e `with` o THEN JUST `the maximum imprisonment on indictment, in months` ELSE NOTHING
        `maximum imprisonment on summary conviction, in months` IS
            CONSIDER c's `the offence facts`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN IF `an offence under s 21 is committed in` e `with` o THEN JUST (`the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction, in months, for` o) ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        e MEANS c's `the employment`
